# Vampire Lord — an Intermediate enemy of the 1997 game, the deck as the original shipped it.
# tier: 5/12 Intermediate enemies — 18 life, bribe 80 gold
# enemy: Vampire Lord (1997 in-game name, s30/assets/text/Advstrings.txt @CREATURENAMES)
# designer: Coyote Tex, MicroProse designer/producer — every enemy deck (precon page, ref. 2)
# variant: Original (base game; the enemy deck files are dated 19 September 1996)
# source: ../shandalar-src/Decks.zip:Decks/0220.dck "Vampire Lord (B, 4th)" [Tier 3 — Manalink 3
#   file dated 2016-02-15; its first 11 maindeck lines are the 1997 deck, the 11 lines (60
#   cards) after them are the modern deck Manalink appended and are NOT shipped; its
#   .vNone/.v<Colour> sections are the 1997 colour-keyed swaps]
# source: ../s30/assets/configs/rogues/vampire_lord.toml (main_cards, sideboard_cards, level 5)
#   [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix above]
# source: ../mage-go/rogue_dck/vampire_lord.dck [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix]
# cross-check: https://mtg.wiki/page/Shandalar_Enemy_Decks_(Intermediate) — "Vampire Lord"
#   (Original) [Tier-web — maindeck agrees]
# group: 1997 originals
name: Vampire Lord
22 Swamp
4 Dark Ritual
3 Mana Vault
4 Animate Dead
4 Weakness
4 Sengir Vampire
4 Sorceress Queen
4 Carrion Ants
4 Vampire Bats
2 Uncle Istvan
2 Terror
3 Howling Mine
# The 1997 file's colour-keyed sideboard sections. The AI played the maindeck WITHOUT
# .vNone plus the one section matching the player's deck colour (.vNone by default);
# .vNone is folded into the maindeck above, and SB: holds, per name, the largest
# colour-section count minus the .vNone count — the smallest sideboard from which
# every 1997 configuration can be rebuilt by swapping.
#   .vNone   3 Howling Mine
#   .vBlack  3 Howling Mine
#   .vBlue   3 Howling Mine
#   .vGreen  3 Black Knight
#   .vRed    3 Winter Orb
#   .vWhite  3 Black Knight
SB: 3 Black Knight
SB: 3 Winter Orb
